  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37780016",
      "title": "LangChain - First Steps",
      "sourceHash": "263a338bf4da904eab8cb6a2b25e57a606b1704cd4ffb6b815b148870d242c23",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "So LangChain is a framework that allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 8.31,
          "en": "to build your own automated AI tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.31,
          "end": 9.45,
          "en": "And for that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.45,
          "end": 14.45,
          "en": "I'll start by creating an email generator tool in Python.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.51,
          "end": 20.16,
          "en": "Therefore, I created this email_generator.py file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.16,
          "end": 23.46,
          "en": "And in this file we should start by importing something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.46,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "from this LangChain package which we installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 30.136,
          "en": "To be precise, from a part of that package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.136,
          "end": 35.136,
          "en": "and that part is the llms package, the llms subpage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.73,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 40.98,
          "en": "From there, we want to import OpenAI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.98,
          "end": 42.54,
          "en": "Now that's simply a thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.54,
          "end": 46.353,
          "en": "a class to be precise, provided by LangChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.49,
          "end": 52.49,
          "en": "You can use this to create an OpenAI instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "as you could call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 58.29,
          "en": "which then later can be used to send requests to OpenAI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.29,
          "end": 61.71,
          "en": "So LangChain needs this OpenAI instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.71,
          "end": 66.12,
          "en": "to send requests to the OpenAI APIs later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 67.5,
          "en": "So indeed here, as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 69,
          "en": "we will have to write some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "because as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 73.65,
          "en": "using LangChain does require some coding skills",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.65,
          "end": 77.37,
          "en": "because it is a thing, a framework, that's meant to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.37,
          "end": 79.11,
          "en": "as part of your own programs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 82.08,
          "en": "so that you can create your own AI workflows.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.08,
          "end": 83.71600000000001,
          "en": "Using it without coding skills",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.71600000000001,
          "end": 86.013,
          "en": "will definitely be challenging.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.09,
          "end": 89.97,
          "en": "Now, when setting up this OpenAI thing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.97,
          "end": 92.07,
          "en": "to be used by LangChain,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.07,
          "end": 95.28,
          "en": "you also must pass some so-called arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.28,
          "end": 97.25999999999999,
          "en": "between these parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.25999999999999,
          "end": 99.64,
          "en": "For example, you must set the openai_api_key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "and this should be equal to your API key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 109.56,
          "en": "which you got in your OpenAI API account.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.56,
          "end": 112.28999999999999,
          "en": "Now here I pasted in my key and I'm hiding it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.28999999999999,
          "end": 114.66,
          "en": "so that you can't see it, so that you can't use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.66,
          "end": 117.47999999999999,
          "en": "But of course, you should paste in your key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.47999999999999,
          "end": 120.45,
          "en": "In addition, you can also set up the temperature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.45,
          "end": 123.72,
          "en": "which in the end controls how random",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.72,
          "end": 124.98,
          "en": "or how creative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.98,
          "end": 128.28,
          "en": "the results generated by the GPT models will be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.28,
          "end": 131.37,
          "en": "And here I'll set this to a value of 0.0",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.37,
          "end": 133.44,
          "en": "so that we have very little,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.44,
          "end": 137.01,
          "en": "basically none, you could say, creativity.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.01,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "With that, this OpenAI thing here is configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 142.53,
          "en": "and we're now ready to continue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 144.12,
          "en": "And with LangChain here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.12,
          "end": 147.24,
          "en": "we will continue by also importing something else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.24,
          "end": 150.513,
          "en": "from LangChain and there from the prompts subpackage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 156.333,
          "en": "From there, we import the PromptTemplate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.92000000000002,
          "end": 159.15,
          "en": "and as the name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.15,
          "end": 162.39,
          "en": "this is a thing which we'll use to construct prompts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.39,
          "end": 167.39,
          "en": "that will be sent to OpenAI, to these OpenAI APIs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 169.683,
          "en": "so to these GPT models.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.09,
          "end": 175.59,
          "en": "You use the PromptTemplate by executing it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.59,
          "end": 177.81,
          "en": "and you stored a result in a variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 177.81,
          "end": 179.07,
          "en": "with a name of your choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 179.07,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "just as I did it with OpenAI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 183.78,
          "en": "which I stored in a variable called llm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.78,
          "end": 187.113,
          "en": "Here, I'll store my prompt in a variable called prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.31,
          "end": 193.08,
          "en": "And then PromptTemplate takes two main arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.08,
          "end": 197.76,
          "en": "It takes an input_variables argument, which is a list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.76,
          "end": 199.92000000000002,
          "en": "and I'll get back to this list soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.92000000000002,
          "end": 203.94,
          "en": "And a template argument, which is a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.94,
          "end": 208.05,
          "en": "And here I'll use this special Python string type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.05,
          "end": 210.493,
          "en": "which is created with three double quotes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 210.493,
          "end": 213.33100000000002,
          "en": "which simply allows us to split a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.33100000000002,
          "end": 217.623,
          "en": "so text in the end, across multiple lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 218.91,
          "end": 220.62,
          "en": "Now this template here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.62,
          "end": 223.17000000000002,
          "en": "this text which we're about to define here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.17000000000002,
          "end": 227.82,
          "en": "will in the end be the prompt that will be sent to OpenAI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.82,
          "end": 229.38,
          "en": "to the GPT models.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.38,
          "end": 231.84,
          "en": "But of course, this prompt can then be enriched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.84,
          "end": 235.71,
          "en": "with some user data, so that as part of our program,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.71,
          "end": 238.86,
          "en": "we have certain parts that are hard coded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.86,
          "end": 242.49,
          "en": "into this prompt and kind of hidden to the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.49,
          "end": 245.31,
          "en": "who later executes our program",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.31,
          "end": 249,
          "en": "and will have some parts in that prompt that are dynamic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249,
          "end": 251.7,
          "en": "and that are sent by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.7,
          "end": 255.09,
          "en": "And this simply allows us to send a predefined prompt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.09,
          "end": 256.8,
          "en": "to OpenAI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.8,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "And we could do the same without LangChain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 262.592,
          "en": "just by using the OpenAI APIs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.592,
          "end": 265.44,
          "en": "as you learned it early in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.44,
          "end": 268.68,
          "en": "But using LangChain can simplify the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 268.68,
          "end": 270.45,
          "en": "of defining such templates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.45,
          "end": 273.12,
          "en": "And in addition, as you will learn later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.12,
          "end": 276.359,
          "en": "LangChain also offers some other nice features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.359,
          "end": 279.24,
          "en": "which in the end simplify the process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.24,
          "end": 282.03,
          "en": "of building automated AI tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.03,
          "end": 284.97,
          "en": "You could build the same tools without LangChain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 284.97,
          "end": 288,
          "en": "but it would require a bit more work from your side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288,
          "end": 291.12,
          "en": "And that's the main idea behind LangChain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.12,
          "end": 293.4,
          "en": "Here, we're going to start simple though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.4,
          "end": 296.553,
          "en": "and we're just going to define such a template now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ],
